From 11eba60588378de080e83c743c13be2adbd76981 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marek 'seqre' Grzelak <git@seqre.dev>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:01:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: x1-acer-swift-14: fix PS8830 retimer reset
 polarity

The reset line of the Parade PS8830 USB-C retimers is active-low, but
both retimer nodes describe it as GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH. The ps883x driver
releases reset by setting the line's logical value to 0, which with the
wrong polarity drives the pin low and keeps the retimer in reset.

The retimer then does not respond on I2C, so every mode switch fails:

  ps883x_retimer 3-0008: failed to write conn_status_0: -6
  pmic_glink_altmode.pmic_glink_altmode pmic_glink.altmode.0: failed to setup retimer to DP: -6

As a result, USB-C docks fall back to USB 2.0 and DisplayPort alt mode
never comes up, so external monitors are not detected.

Use GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW, as the ThinkPad T14s and the X1E CRD do for the
same pins (pm8550_gpios 10 and tlmm 176).

Tested on an Acer Swift Go 14 AI (SFG14-01) with a USB-C dock: the
retimer errors are gone, the dock enumerates at 10 Gbps, and the
external monitor comes up on DP-1 at 3840x2160.

Fixes: 3d76671d75c2 ("UBUNTU: SAUCE: arm64: dts: qcom: x1-acer-swift-14: Add support for Acer Swift 14")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-acer-swift-14.dtsi | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-acer-swift-14.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-acer-swift-14.dtsi
index 67d2825..be73f6a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-acer-swift-14.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-acer-swift-14.dtsi
@@ -753,7 +753,7 @@ typec-mux@8 {
 		vddat-supply = <&vreg_rtmr0_1p15>;
 		vddio-supply = <&vreg_rtmr0_1p8>;
 
-		reset-gpios = <&pm8550_gpios 10 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		reset-gpios = <&pm8550_gpios 10 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 
 		retimer-switch;
 		orientation-switch;
@@ -856,7 +856,7 @@ typec-mux@8 {
 		vddat-supply = <&vreg_rtmr1_1p15>;
 		vddio-supply = <&vreg_rtmr1_1p8>;
 
-		reset-gpios = <&tlmm 176 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		reset-gpios = <&tlmm 176 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 
 		retimer-switch;
 		orientation-switch;
-- 
2.53.0

